METHOD: fsPromises.readFile (or fs.readFile when using the promises API)
MODULE: node:fs/promises (or node:fs)
EXAMPLE: 
```javascript
import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';

async function example() {
  try {
    const data = await readFile('/path/to/file.txt', { encoding: 'utf8' });
    console.log(data);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Error reading file:', err);
  }
}

example();
```
NOTES: Modern Node.js best practices recommend using the `node:fs/promises` API (`fsPromises.readFile`) with `async/await` rather than the legacy callback-based `fs.readFile` or synchronous methods for non-blocking asynchronous file reading.
